I decided to move the logic into its own file called `RuleConstraintSemantics.java`. I will rename this once I can think of a better name. Your `IncompatibleDeterminingHelper.java` suggestion is not a bad idea. I will use that if I can't think of anything better.

As for reimplementing behaviour, we previously used `ruleContext.targetPlatformHasConstraint()`:
https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/d2750262695b1cef7365e5491711ce411cd85215/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/analysis/constraints/RuleContextConstraintSemantics.java#L916-L921
which is implemented here:
https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/d2750262695b1cef7365e5491711ce411cd85215/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/analysis/RuleContext.java#L1246-L1251

And now we do this:
```
ImmutableList<ConstraintValueInfo> invalidConstraintValues =
    PlatformProviderUtils.constraintValues(constraintProviders).stream()
        .filter(cv -> !platformInfo.constraints().hasConstraintValue(cv))
        .collect(ImmutableList.toImmutableList());
```

So the behaviour _should_ be the same. I am pretty sure that we're using a different layer of abstraction, but the same underlying logic.

That all being said, minimizing the code as much as possible sounds like a good idea to me. Any help you can provide here is appreciated. I will scour the rest of the code base to see what's available to be re-used.

I remember struggling with de-duplicating the visibility logic because of how early in the analysis phase this code runs. I will also take another look at that.

